dShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-18T17:18:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T17:18:11Z","body":"Closing due to lack of response, if you provide the requested information this can be reopened ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4480091039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4562700152","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118769#issuecomment-4562700152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118769","id":4562700152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABD_VHeA","user":{"login":"duianto","id":13420573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNDIwNTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13420573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto","html_url":"https://github.com/duianto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/duianto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-28T09:41:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T09:49:17Z","body":"Update:\nOpened a new issue here:\nPolygon2d hides when its original shape is panned outside the main viewport #119843\n\n---\n\nThe OP mentions zooming with a camera, but a polygon disappearing issue happens when zooming or panning the main viewport without a camera.\n\n\nReproducible in:\nv4.7.beta3.official [860821708]\n\nNot reproducible in:\nv4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n\nGodot v4.7.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - GeForce GTX 550 Ti - Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-2100 CPU @ 3.10GHz (4 threads) - 11.95 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\nDescription:\nA polygon2d hides unexpectedly, when its initial shape is panned or zoomed outside Godot's main viewport. After the polygon has been moved in the polygon editor.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a8150b1-7ab1-44cb-82be-8287295f03a4\n\nWorkaround:\nClosing and reopening the scene fixes it, until the polygon is moved again in the polygon editor.\n\nReproduction steps:\n- open project: [polygon-2d-hides-when-original-shape-is-outside-main-viewport.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28342025/polygon-2d-hides-when-original-shape-is-outside-main-viewport.zip)\n- the scene panel contains:\n```\nNode2D\n  Polygon2D\n  Polygon2D2\n```\nNote: The issue occurs with only one polygon. The second polygon just makes it easy to see the polygon's original position.\n- select the second child node: Polygon2D2\n- in the bottom polygon editor's top bar, select the move polygon tool\n- in the polygon editor, drag the polygon to the right \n- in Godot's main viewport, pan the viewport, by middle mouse button dragging to the left until the left polygon is outside the viewport\n\nIssue:\nThe right polygon disappears when the left polygon (right polygon's original position) is outside the main viewport.\nThe right polygon appears when the viewport is panned to the right and the left polygon appears again.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a8150b1-7ab1-44cb-82be-8287295f03a4\n\nExpected:\nThe right polygon should use its new position to check if it's outside the main viewport. Like it does in: v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a45c9d00-9eda-495d-8711-c9f7cf4ffb19\n\nMinimal reproduction project (MRP)\n[polygon-2d-hides-when-original-shape-is-outside-main-viewport.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28342025/polygon-2d-hides-when-original-shape-is-outside-main-viewport.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4562700152/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4562711635","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118769#issuecomment-4562711635","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118769","id":4562711635,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABD_V0Uw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-28T09:42:50Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T09:42:50Z","body":"Please open a new issue for this instead to keep it simple ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4562711635/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4615143257","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118769#issuecomment-4615143257","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118769","id":4615143257,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABExV_WQ","user":{"login":"Zamir7","id":8374434,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNzQ0MzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8374434?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7","html_url":"https://github.com/Zamir7","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zamir7/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-03T17:39:47Z","updated_at":"2026-06-03T17:59:46Z","body":"\"The right polygon disappears when the left polygon (the right polygon's original position) is outside the main viewport.\"\n\nYes, and this isn't really a copying issue, but rather a behavior that occurs when the center of gravity (I don't know what it's called, but in the editor it's the red cross relative to which the polygon moves, as in the video above) is in the center. Basically, if the center isn't inside the polygon itself, then as the polygon approaches the screen boundaries, it disappears. Moreover, it all depends on which direction from the center the shift occurred. If it's below, then the top disappears when moving, etc.\n\nYou can use the project kindly provided by duianto as a basis for this example project. If this is possible, I can attach his project if not.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4615143257/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4615966363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118769#issuecomment-4615966363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118769","id":4615966363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEyIOmw","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"n